{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"42472dcba5b6bd72","name":"card_unit_fairey_battle_elit","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Poland/units/card_unit_fairey_battle_elit","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"BATTLE Mk I PL","text":"When you deploy another Exile unit, give it +1+1.","flavorText":"The Fairey Battle was a British light bomber that was produced between 1937-1940 and used during WWII by the RAF and Allied air forces. At the start of the war the Fairey Battle was already obsolete but it remained in frontline service due to lack of replacements. The aircraft was considered easy to fly and it could take damage, but it was no match against the modern German fighters. At the start of the war the Battle was used for reconnaissance missions but later it would be called on for ground attack roles in an desperate attempt to stop the German advance. However, in 1940 most Fairey Battle aircraft had been pulled from frontline service. The Fairey Battle was used by four Polish bomber squadrons in the RAF.","faction":"Poland","type":"bomber","rarity":"Rare","cost":2,"operationCost":1,"attack":1,"defense":2},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_fairey_battle_elit","title":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_unit_fairey_battle_elit_title","SourceString":"BATTLE Mk I PL","LocalizedString":"BATTLE Mk I PL"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::bomber","attack":1,"defense":2,"range":2,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Poland","kredits":2,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_unit_fairey_battle_elit_text","SourceString":"When you deploy another Exile unit, give it +1+1.","LocalizedString":"When you deploy another Exile unit, give it +1+1."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_poland","Key":"card_unit_fairey_battle_elit_history","SourceString":"The Fairey Battle was a British light bomber that was produced between 1937-1940 and used during WWII by the RAF and Allied air forces. At the start of the war the Fairey Battle was already obsolete but it remained in frontline service due to lack of replacements. The aircraft was considered easy to fly and it could take damage, but it was no match against the modern German fighters. At the start of the war the Battle was used for reconnaissance missions but later it would be called on for ground attack roles in an desperate attempt to stop the German advance. However, in 1940 most Fairey Battle aircraft had been pulled from frontline service. The Fairey Battle was used by four Polish bomber squadrons in the RAF.","LocalizedString":"The Fairey Battle was a British light bomber that was produced between 1937-1940 and used during WWII by the RAF and Allied air forces. At the start of the war the Fairey Battle was already obsolete but it remained in frontline service due to lack of replacements. The aircraft was considered easy to fly and it could take damage, but it was no match against the modern German fighters. At the start of the war the Battle was used for reconnaissance missions but later it would be called on for ground attack roles in an desperate attempt to stop the German advance. However, in 1940 most Fairey Battle aircraft had been pulled from frontline service. The Fairey Battle was used by four Polish bomber squadrons in the RAF."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Rare","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::Legions","isReserved":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardPlayedFromHand"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Exile"],"exileNation":"EFactionEnum::Britain","soundBlowUp":{"ObjectName":"SoundWave'Explosion_Small'","ObjectPath":"kards/Content/Assets/Audio/Misc/Explosion_Small.0"},"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Britain/Invasion/t_fairy_battle.t_fairy_battle","SubPathString":""},"artist":"Jarosław Wróbel","historyPhoto":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/HistoricalPhotos/FAIREY_BATTLE.FAIREY_BATTLE","SubPathString":""},"historyPhotoSize":{"X":512.0,"Y":250.0},"historyPho